==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From [[:w:Tuxedo Park, New York|Tuxedo Park, New York]], USA, where the fashion is often said to have originated.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|tŭksē'dō}}, {{IPA|/tʌkˈsiːdoʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/tʌkˈsiːdəʊ/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
[[Image:Men in black tie.jpg|thumb|right|Three men in tuxedos]]
{{en-noun|tuxedos|tuxedoes}}

# A typically [[black]] [[formal]] [[jacket]] worn by men.
# The entire [[suit]] complementing and including this jacket.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|formal jacket}} {{l|en|dinner jacket}}
* {{sense|formal suit}} {{l|en|black tie}}, {{l|en|tux}}, {{l|en|penguin suit}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|tux}}
* {{l|en|tuxedo cat}}
* {{l|en|Canadian tuxedo}}
* {{l|en|Texan tuxedo}}

